    "body": "D2 [BLACK] — METAL / ACCENT FOCAL-ISLAND TRANSFER R01\n\nMODE = EXISTING-SOURCE FORENSICS ONLY\nIMAGE GENERATION/EDIT/REDRAW = NO\nCUSTOM CODE / WRAPPER / GLUE = NO\nHEAD = `2b0438cb817d41e53bec23944af7237893e12b4b`\n\nSOURCES:\n- C00-A Duncan costume/detail sheet\n- C00-C Duncan master front\n- TEX-TEACHER-01 changed-character texture teacher sample (`1 Гаммот.png`, SHA256 already recorded as `d0ed48cc8ca1e7053e9272948431f667f644e0a64bd48c3ecd4e47196de64277`)\n\n## DUNCAN GOLD / SILVER SCALE TRANSFER\n\nC00-A close/detail evidence:\n- gold wristwatch carries bracelet-link segmentation, bezel, dial marks, hands and date-window information;\n- gold belt hardware/buttons read through compact warm shape + hard value edge;\n- silver earrings preserve ring + long spike construction.\n\nC00-C full-body evidence:\n- watch collapses to a small compact gold/bright wrist accent; most internal dial/bracelet micro-information no longer carries the read;\n- buttons collapse to simple gold disks/points;\n- chain collapses to a thin warm line;\n- silver earrings preserve the long vertical silhouette more strongly than any internal metal texture.\n\nSupported order:\n`METAL ACCENT SCALE SURVIVAL = SHAPE / COLOR-ACCENT / SPECULAR-EDGE > PANEL/CONSTRUCTION > MICRO-ORNAMENT`\n\n## CHANGED-CHARACTER TRANSFER: TEX-TEACHER-01\n\nThe changed design gives the same higher-level behavior:\n- ornate gold is concentrated as local line-network/detail islands on large calm black fields;\n- steel mask/weapon read first from hard panel geometry, silhouette and compact specular/value jumps;\n- scratches/rivets/surface damage are secondary to metal form;\n- black clothing remains the quiet carrier field around high-frequency gold/metal accents.\n\nThis supports a cross-character principle without transferring the teacher sample's gothic motifs, weapon, mask, creature or exact embroidery design.\n\n## PROVISIONAL RULES\n\n`GOLD = SPARSE FOCAL ISLAND / COLOR + SHAPE FIRST`\n\n`SILVER EARRING = SILHOUETTE FIRST / INTERNAL TEXTURE NEAR-ZERO`\n\n`STEEL = FORM/PANEL -> HARD EDGE -> SPECULAR -> SPARSE DAMAGE`\n\n`HIGH DETAIL REQUIRES CALM SURROUNDING FIELD`\n\nDistance routing:\n- CLOSE: construction + selected ornament/specular;\n- MID: simple gold/silver/steel shapes + one or few highlight cues;\n- FAR: tiny accent or silhouette only; internal ornament disappears.\n\nFAIL modes:\n- metallic grain everywhere;\n- glitter/sparkle noise;\n- scratches used as the primary definition of metal;\n- gold spread uniformly across costume;\n- ornament retaining identical density at all scales;\n- metal accents competing with face/silhouette hierarchy.\n\n## STATUS\n\n`METAL_FOCAL_ISLAND_RULE_R01 = PARTIAL / CHANGED-CHARACTER TRANSFER SUPPORTED`\n\n`EXACT NUMERIC METAL ENVELOPE = NOT PROVEN`\n\n`TEXTURE_LANGUAGE_R01 = NOT PASS`\n\nNo canon lock, no production activation, no model-weight claim, no merge authority.\n\nNEXT = resolve HAIR source contradiction and continue scale/material authority routing using existing sources + mature OSS only.",
